# Images and Assets

## Product imagery is first-class content

Treat product images as core content, not decorative filler.

Where Sanity is used, use Sanity's image pipeline/CDN and request appropriate sizes/crops.

## Image roles

Define consistent treatment for:
- hero images
- product thumbnails
- product detail gallery
- article/recipe imagery
- testimonial or team images

## Cropping

Choose crop behavior intentionally.
Do not use one universal `object-cover` rule for every photograph.

Keep important produce centered or positioned according to the composition of the source image.

## Aspect ratios

Use consistent aspect ratio variants so catalogue grids remain aligned.

Do not allow one product card to become dramatically taller solely because the source image has a different ratio.

## Optimization

Use responsive image sizes.
Avoid shipping desktop-sized images to small screens.

Prefer modern formats supported by the platform.

Always reserve image space to avoid layout shift.

## Placeholder strategy

Do not use generic random stock images as final content.
If an asset is missing during development, use a clearly identifiable placeholder and make the CMS field easy to replace.

## Decorative imagery

Decorative imagery must not compete with product discovery or CTA hierarchy.
